        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 1 at 8:22AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "The river crested at 40.44 ft at 4:30am & is falling. As a result of\nthe release, debris in the water remains possible on the Taku River,\nextending down Taku Inlet, & into Stephens Passage, & the water\ntemperature in that area may also still be colder than normal\nthrough tonight.\n\n\nFor Taku River near Juneau:\nAt 7:00am the stage was 40.3 feet & falling.\nForecast: Water levels will continue to fall through tonight.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
